=====================================================================
SECTION 5: Quick Notes & Fun Facts
=====================================================================

    - Topo Sort + Relaxation handles NEGATIVE weights in DAGs — since DAGs
      have no cycles, negative weights can't create infinite loops.
      It's also the fastest single-source algo at O(V+E).

    - Dijkstra FAILS with negative weights because once it "finalizes" a
      node's distance, it never revisits it. A negative edge could later
      provide a shorter path that Dijkstra already skipped.

    - Bellman-Ford detects negative cycles by running V-1 relaxation passes.
      If distances still decrease on the V-th pass → negative cycle exists.

    - Floyd-Warshall uses DP: for each intermediate node k, check if going
      through k gives a shorter path: dist[i][j] = min(dist[i][j], dist[i][k] + dist[k][j])

    - 0-1 BFS optimization: push weight-0 edges to the FRONT of a deque,
      weight-1 edges to the BACK. This avoids the overhead of a priority queue.
